    "reviewedMeaning": {
      "index": "The trigger index selects Triggers; its AreaPointStart and AreaPointNum select a closed ring from Points.",
      "queryAxes": "The query Vector3.x and Vector3.z compare with stored Coord.X and Coord.Y; Vector3.y compares with stored height limits.",
      "bounds": "For finite values, the minimum and maximum horizontal and height comparisons include equality.",
      "polygon": "The unpatched branch toggles even-odd parity when the endpoints' stored Coord.Y comparisons straddle query Z and the edge's positive-X ray intersection is strictly greater than query X.",
      "boundary": "The rectangle and height limits are inclusive; points exactly on a polygon edge need separate case analysis and are not asserted inside."
    }
  },
  "evidenceBoundary": {
    "exact": "The selected native input hashes, metadata method identities and complete pointer-gap code windows are revalidated before naming fields.",
    "direct": "Generated FlatBuffer indexed accessors return int32 or fixed structs; getter code reads the recorded struct offsets. The current payload vectors and inline bounds use those widths. The selected unpatched CheckInArea body reads a trigger's point span, compares query Vector3 X/Z and Y with horizontal and height bounds, and evaluates even-odd ray crossings over the stored ring; the separately pinned toggle-off window completes the parity branch.",
    "structuralOnly": "Area visibility and trigger point spans are authored index relations in the serialized data; XY containment is checked against serialized bounds.",
